      {
        "line": 355,
        "text": "### 9.1 Portfolio drawdown objective"
      },
      {
        "line": 357,
        "text": "A portfolio peak-to-trough drawdown of approximately **20%** is a **soft risk-tolerance and escalation threshold**, not a guaranteed maximum loss, stop-loss rul"
      },
      {
        "line": 367,
        "text": "- sell high-quality holdings merely because portfolio drawdown approaches 20%;"
      },
      {
        "line": 371,
        "text": "Risk response must identify the **source of drawdown** before prescribing action. The review should distinguish among:"
      },
      {
        "line": 384,
        "text": "Market-driven drawdown and business-driven permanent impairment must not be treated as the same risk event."
      },
      {
        "line": 390,
        "text": "However, volatility and drawdown remain relevant because they affect capital availability, concentration, behavioral discipline, and portfolio resilience."
      },
      {
        "line": 634,
        "text": "Material changes to investment universe, use of leverage, return objective, drawdown philosophy, investment horizon, or core investment style require explicit p"
      },
      {
        "line": 692,
        "text": "- exact drawdown response ladder;"
      },
      {
        "line": 718,
        "text": "- portfolio drawdown target;"
      },
      {
        "line": 741,
        "text": "10. **20% drawdown is a soft escalation threshold, not a stop-loss.** Drawdown must trigger diagnosis of its source; market beta and permanent business impairme"
      }
    ]
