  {
    "path": "docs/01 SYSTEM/RISK_POLICY_v1.0.md",
    "sha256": "3785c1bb39b80435655a1621b2afbda992c38beaff82edebc0c67b0bc54ee744",
    "anchors": [
      {
        "line": 15,
        "text": "This Risk Policy is the authoritative source of portfolio risk limits, hard risk vetoes, escalation rules, concentration controls, drawdown response, cash-reser"
      },
      {
        "line": 23,
        "text": "- drawdown escalation rules;"
      },
      {
        "line": 62,
        "text": "- **temporary mark-to-market drawdown**;"
      },
      {
        "line": 141,
        "text": "The portfolio-level drawdown objective is to keep peak-to-trough drawdown **around or below 20% under normal adverse market conditions**, as stated in `INVESTME"
      },
      {
        "line": 145,
        "text": "The system must never sell a fundamentally sound security solely because portfolio drawdown crosses a numerical threshold."
      },
      {
        "line": 149,
        "text": "Portfolio drawdown must be measured on a **cash-flow-adjusted basis** so that monthly DCA contributions or withdrawals do not artificially create or erase drawd"
      },
      {
        "line": 168,
        "text": "Until Milestone 2 implements the formal NAV model, every drawdown calculation must explicitly state:"
      },
      {
        "line": 192,
        "text": "1. identify whether drawdown is market-wide, sector-driven, concentration-driven, or thesis-specific;"
      },
      {
        "line": 193,
        "text": "2. review top contributors to drawdown;"
      },
      {
        "line": 204,
        "text": "2. mandatory review of all positions contributing materially to drawdown;"
      },
      {
        "line": 218,
        "text": "1. classify the source of drawdown;"
      },
      {
        "line": 226,
        "text": "A CRITICAL drawdown does **not** automatically require broad portfolio liquidation."
      },
      {
        "line": 246,
        "text": "The **Current Drawdown Band** is determined only by the current cash-flow-adjusted drawdown level."
      },
      {
        "line": 254,
        "text": "A recovery in NAV immediately changes the Current Drawdown Band according to the measured drawdown, even if a prior WATCH / ELEVATED / CRITICAL / SEVERE review "
      },
      {
        "line": 423,
        "text": "- drawdown / escalation constraints;"
      },
      {
        "line": 441,
        "text": "- no drawdown, concentration, or risk-escalation rule requires additional liquidity;"
      }
    ]
  },
